actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22556","marks":["code"],"text":"from_outcome"},{"id":"spn-22557","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22558","marks":["code"],"text":"from_feedback"},{"id":"spn-22559","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22560","marks":["code"],"text":"detect_novelty"},{"id":"spn-22561","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22562","marks":["code"],"text":"from_interaction"},{"id":"spn-22563","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22564","marks":["code"],"text":"contradictions"}]},{"id":"blk-22421","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22565","marks":["code"],"text":"consolidate"},{"id":"spn-22566","text":" — \"Clean up\" (4 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22422","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22567","marks":["code"],"text":"run"},{"id":"spn-22568","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22569","marks":["code"],"text":"stats"},{"id":"spn-22570","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22571","marks":["code"],"text":"query"},{"id":"spn-22572","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22573","marks":["code"],"text":"traverse"}]},{"id":"blk-22423","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22574","text":"Combined Impact"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-22425","spans":[{"id":"spn-22575","text":"Scenario"}]},{"id":"blk-22426","spans":[{"id":"spn-22576","text":"Before"}]},{"id":"blk-22427","spans":[{"id":"spn-22577","text":"After"}]}],"id":"blk-22424","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-22428","spans":[{"id":"spn-22578","text":"Graphonomous alone"}]},{"id":"blk-22429","spans":[{"id":"spn-22579","text":"29 tools"}]},{"id":"blk-22430","spans":[{"id":"spn-22580","text":"5 tools"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22431","spans":[{"id":"spn-22581","text":"PRISM alone"}]},{"id":"blk-22432","spans":[{"id":"spn-22582","text":"47 tools"}]},{"id":"blk-22433","spans":[{"id":"spn-22583","text":"6 tools"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22434","spans":[{"id":"spn-22584","text":"Both in same session"}]},{"id":"blk-22435","spans":[{"id":"spn-22585","text":"76 tools"}]},{"id":"blk-22436","spans":[{"id":"spn-22586","text":"11 tools"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-22437","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22587","text":"Context savings: ~85% reduction in tool schema tokens. Selection accuracy: from ~49% (76 tools) to ~95% (11 tools)."}]},{"id":"blk-22438","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22588","text":"Implementation"}]},{"id":"blk-22439","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22589","text":"Both systems use the same Elixir pattern: a single Anubis.Server.Component module per machine with an "},{"id":"spn-22590","marks":["code"],"text":"action"},{"id":"spn-22591","text":" field that dispatches internally to the existing tool implementations. The v1 tool modules are preserved as the implementation layer."}]},{"id":"blk-22440","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22592","text":"See:"}]},{"id":"blk-22441","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22443","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22593","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous/lib/graphonomous/mcp/machines/"},{"id":"spn-22594","text":" — Graphonomous machine modules"}]}],"id":"blk-22442","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22445","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22595","marks":["code"],"text":"PRISM/lib/prism/mcp/machines/"},{"id":"spn-22596","text":" — PRISM machine modules"}]}],"id":"blk-22444","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22597","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/prompts/DUAL_LOOP_MACHINES.md"},{"id":"spn-22598","text":" — canonical architecture design"}]}],"id":"blk-22446","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-22448","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22599","text":"Triple loop and beyond — PULSE generalization"}]},{"id":"blk-22449","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22600","text":"The Graphonomous ↔ PRISM dual loop is the canonical example, but the [&] ecosystem actually runs "},{"id":"spn-22601","marks":["bold"],"text":"at least three"},{"id":"spn-22602","text":" nested loops today:"}]},{"id":"blk-22450","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"PRISM (outer)        compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose\n  │\n  └─ Graphonomous    retrieve → route → act → learn → consolidate\n       │\n       └─ Deliberation    survey → triage → dispatch → act → learn"},{"id":"blk-22451","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22603","text":"OS-010 PULSE encodes this nesting in each manifest's "},{"id":"spn-22604","marks":["code"],"text":"nesting"},{"id":"spn-22605","text":" block:"}]},{"id":"blk-22452","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22606","marks":["code"],"text":"prism.benchmark"},{"id":"spn-22607","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-22608","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.continual_learning]"}]}],"id":"blk-22453","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22456","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22609","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.continual_learning"},{"id":"spn-22610","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-22611","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.deliberate]"},{"id":"spn-22612","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-22613","marks":["code"],"text":"parent_loop: prism.benchmark"}]}],"id":"blk-22455","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22458","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22614","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-22615","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-22616","marks":["code"],"text":"parent_loop: graphonomous.continual_learning"}]}],"id":"blk-22457","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-22459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22617","text":"PULSE supports unbounded nesting depth. OS-008 (Agent Harness, draft) is expected to add a fourth outer layer that wraps PRISM itself — when it ships, the only change required is a new manifest with "},{"id":"spn-22618","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [prism.benchmark]"},{"id":"spn-22619","text":". No code changes to existing machines."}]},{"id":"blk-22460","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22620","text":"Why this matters for the machine architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-22461","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22621","text":"The 5/6/11-tool count documented above is a "},{"id":"spn-22622","marks":["bold"],"text":"floor"},{"id":"spn-22623","text":", not a ceiling. Adding a third loop adds at most 5 more machines (one per phase kind), and because PULSE manifests declare the inner-loop boundary explicitly, the outer machines do not need to learn about inner machines individually. PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-22624","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-22625","text":" machine, for example, drives any PULSE-conforming inner loop through its declared "},{"id":"spn-22626","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-22627","text":" phase — it does not need a Graphonomous-specific code path."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-22463","spans":[{"id":"spn-22628","text":"Layers in session"}]},{"id":"blk-22464","spans":[{"id":"spn-22629","text":"Tool count (machines)"}]},{"id":"blk-22465","spans":[{"id":"spn-22630","text":"Tool count (legacy v1)"}]}],"id":"blk-22462","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-22466","spans":[{"id":"spn-22631","text":"Graphonomous alone"}]},{"id":"blk-22467","spans":[{"id":"spn-22632","text":"5"}]},{"id":"blk-22468","spans":[{"id":"spn-22633","text":"29"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22469","spans":[{"id":"spn-22634","text":"Graphonomous + PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-22470","spans":[{"id":"spn-22635","text":"11"}]},{"id":"blk-22471","spans":[{"id":"spn-22636","text":"76"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22472","spans":[{"id":"spn-22637","text":"Graphonomous + PRISM + OS-008 Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-22473","spans":[{"id":"spn-22638","text":"~16"}]},{"id":"blk-22474","spans":[{"id":"spn-22639","text":"~100+"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22475","spans":[{"id":"spn-22640","text":"Graphonomous + PRISM + OS-008 + AgenTroMatic deliberation"}]},{"id":"blk-22476","spans":[{"id":"spn-22641","text":"~21"}]},{"id":"blk-22477","spans":[{"id":"spn-22642","text":"~130+"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-22478","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22643","text":"The savings compound with depth, and PULSE's manifest standard is what makes the composition algebraic instead of ad-hoc."}]},{"id":"blk-22479","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22644","text":"Three-protocol stack at runtime"}]},{"id":"blk-22480","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM    — measures loops over time      (diagnostic)   │ OS-009\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE    — declares loops + circulation   (temporal)    │ OS-010\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&]      — composes capabilities          (structural)  │ AmpersandBoxDesign\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-22481","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22645","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-22646","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-22647","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-22648","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-22649","text":" and its runtime passes all 12 conformance tests. A system is "},{"id":"spn-22650","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-22651","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-22652","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-22653","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-22654","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-22655","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-22656","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-22657","text":" phase. No bespoke per-system integration required."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierahdzpgxfmslohmzycfooly4p4iyuaxgf2l7jjsxsmaq2ugwi3bgkq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}